# No Command-K Search Shortcuts

Do not add `Cmd+K`, `Ctrl+K`, or `⌘K` search shortcuts in any project unless the user explicitly requests that behavior in the current task.

## Default Requirements

- Do not register keyboard handlers for `metaKey/ctrlKey + k`.
- Do not render UI shortcut badges/hints like `⌘K`, `Ctrl+K`, or `Command + K`.
- If a search input needs global focus behavior, use non-colliding patterns (for example `/`) only when requested.
- When updating existing code, remove `Cmd/Ctrl+K` handlers and displayed hints unless the user explicitly asks to keep them.

## Re-introduction Gate

Only add this feature when the user clearly asks for Command/Ctrl+K support in the current conversation.
